WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:09.140
Processing Integrity addresses whether systems process information completely, accurately, timely, and according to expectations.

2
00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:13.100
Customers rely on systems to perform intended functions correctly.

3
00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:20.960
If a service transforms, calculates, routes, or reports information, the correctness of that processing matters.

4
00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:31.000
Software testing, validation, quality assurance, automation, reconciliation, and change management all help support processing integrity objectives.

5
00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:36.320
For engineers, processing integrity connects product quality to trust.

6
00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:44.420
Good design, clear requirements, controlled changes, and meaningful testing help ensure the system behaves as intended.
